  * SWEET PM6150L L11C bring-up; see report.md for DT and source evidence.
  * Sole XNU apps-DRV owner, called from thread context with deep idle disabled.
  * No sleep/wake programming, SPMI writes, GIC handler, or timeout recovery.
+ *
+ * vayu (SM8150) has the same apps RSC (dt mailbox@18220000 "apps_rsc": 0x18220000 + TCS 0x18220d00,
+ * drv-id 2, tcs-config ACTIVE 2 / SLEEP 3 / WAKE 3 / CONTROL 1) and cmd-db locator (0xc3f000c).
+ * Boot-arg sweetbw=1 also votes the DDR and system-cache bus clock managers (BCM "MC0", "SH0")
+ * to their highest level, as an active-only request: without a bus driver nobody asks RPMh for
+ * bandwidth and CoreAnimation's CPU renderer is memory-bound. A copy of 16 MB is timed before
+ * and after the vote.
  */
